{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/138504-what-have-you-done-with-a-mummy-game","id":138504,"title":"What have you done with a Mummy game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-15T15:50:57-07:00","id":138504,"title":"What have you done with a Mummy game?","content":"I want to like this game, but just have such a hard time imagining what to do with it, either as a player or a GM. I am looking for your experiences, preferably positive, though negative are also helpful.<br /> <br /> My thanks to any and all who respond. Except spambots. Fuck those guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T16:41:27-07:00","id":138594,"title":"","content":"There's a few AP threads on this forum and on rpg.net, as well as Christian A's 1001 Mummy Plot Hooks thread.<br /> <br /> Pick any film, television show, book, or game where a protagonist has amnesia. Ready, set, go","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T17:51:10-07:00","id":138676,"title":"","content":"I noticed that Mummy takes a while to gather momentum at first. theres a lot of material to digest, and with Mummies waking up so at the mercy of the storyteller, and so little to go with at first, it can be hard. However, I noticed that it builds up over time, especially as more supplements are released. Occasional flashbacks, name drops, and vague vibes can become goldmines for later plot hooks. I'll admit, the majority of my game was flashbacks for a while. But now, I'm DROWNING in plot hooks. Past life versions of cultists.. changes in friends over their descents.. hints about Deceived (what they are or what theyre doing).. Dreams of Avarice.. it really is lovely. And it does deliver on the concept of Memory--by now, mummies who started clumsily and automated have become very human, as have their stories. Gone are the days of rampaging after relics--now its about trying to deal with falling in love with a mortal, dealing with the deaths (even if only temporary) of loved ones, trying to figure out who you are.. Its a mortal game on the scale of millenia, and 6000 years is a lot of room for flashbacks, plothooks, and epic events in life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T22:17:04-07:00","id":138947,"title":"","content":"The fun thing about Mummy is that it's a game about history, where you get to play a character who was there, who's witnessed it all. Pick any interesting historical event you like. Your mummy was there. Build a story hook around it. Done.<br /> <br /> Also, as reseru said, I recommend checking out my 1001 story hooks thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T00:58:53-07:00","id":139099,"title":"","content":"My current chronicle of Mummy sees the meret waking in Constantinople just prior to the Third Turn. Their tomb is being robbed, but more alarmingly (once they've dealt with the robbers) they notice that their intricate hieroglyphs and tableaus around the room all have one common feature: the heads and faces have been chipped away. Additionally, there's another sarcophagus in there will them, but it hangs empty.<br /> <br /> As the meret stumble out into Constantinople for the first time in around a millennium (they remember Alexander the Great, to a degree) they are trying to piece together their pasts, what drew them here from Alexandria, who their missing companion is, why they're missing, how this ties in to every other meret in this nome seemingly being banished to this city and who it is that sent these tomb robbers to their tomb in the first place.<br /> <br /> All in all, I count it among the best games I've ever run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","user":"The Gentleman Gamer","date":". 05-16-2014, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T04:00:02-07:00","id":139163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/138504-what-have-you-done-with-a-mummy-game?p=139099#post139099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All in all, I count it among the best games I've ever run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very awesome to hear, considering watching some of your old videos just re-sold me on <i>Anima: Beyond Fantasy</i> a few days ago <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T05:11:50-07:00","id":139204,"title":"","content":"It's been a long time since I played Anima now. It's a game with a simple d% mechanic and yet has a ridiculous amount of algorithms behind it. Playing a spellcaster is fun, but needlessly complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T06:17:55-07:00","id":139239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/138504-what-have-you-done-with-a-mummy-game?p=139204#post139204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but needlessly complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>The more time goes on, the less I like crunchy mechanics and wow <i>Anima</i> is crunchy! I like WoD because, even if it's not right in the middle of the Crunch Scale, I feel comfortable ditching rules and dice entirely if it'll end up as more fun for us. I guess you can have that attitude with any game, but I also guess WoD is what made me realize it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T06:48:10-07:00","id":140469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/138504-what-have-you-done-with-a-mummy-game#post138504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to like this game, but just have such a hard time imagining what to do with it, either as a player or a GM. I am looking for your experiences, preferably positive, though negative are also helpful.<br /> <br /> My thanks to any and all who respond. Except spambots. Fuck those guys.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/messages/boards/forum/8344542\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/messages/boards/forum/8344542\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/messages/boards/forum/8344542\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/messages/boards/forum/8344542 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T21:23:41-07:00","id":147543,"title":"","content":"I've only run the adventure in the back of the core book, but I had a good time with it and my group mostly did too. What struck me with the focus on tombs, their defenses in game terms, recovering relics from their improper owners, and powers like Palace Knows Its Pharaoh with their focus on specific buildings, is that Mummy has a lot of room for classic tomb-raiding, dare I say dungeon-crawling action. I added a scene when one of the PCs was infiltrating O Pardal Vermelho's tomb based on the stats provided, crawling through corridors and dodging traps and having a nice memorable moment balancing over a pit of crawling scarabs and deciding whether to continue to the objective or risk overextending herself to swipe a relic that had been left there for safekeeping. I think you could have a lot of fun with a big physical action setpiece infiltrating some secure corporate headquarters Shadowrun-style to get to the real challenge, a trap-laden and magically warded tomb complex in the sub-basement.<br /> <br /> Another possibility: I told myself I would explain Mummy to someone by having them watch this video, so i'll encourage you to take inspiration from this exciting scene featuring the King of Pop himself. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LeiFF0gvqcc\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LeiFF0gvqcc</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}